      "caption": "The Emender head-type taxonomy:eigenvalue placement×saturation.(A)Each head is fixed by where its along-keyeigenvalue sits in the complex unit disk— real-positivedecay,real-negativereflect, or complexrot— and by whether the statemap is linear or saturated. The orange real diameter is the locusGDN-2 occupies.(B)The two axes name five cells. Shading marksGDN-2-adjacent linear cores; the Emender also explores off-axisrotation(rot) and saturated state maps(nonlin) as a within-layerpool. This taxonomy is descriptive:different decay placementprevents an exact equal-parameter restriction of the production cores.rot-nonlinis reserved for future work. The GDN-2 corner of this grid isthe mixer of the 1.3 B linear baseline of(GDN2), selected by the same search protocol as E97."
